Vendor: FreeType's BDF and synthesis functions on every system.

zebkit's package ships <freetype/ftbdf.h> and <freetype/ftsynth.h> on
Linux, macOS and Windows, and exports FreeType's functions under
zebkit_vendor_freetype_*. Chromium compiles ftbdf.c and ftsynth.c only for
Linux, ChromeOS and Cast, so on macOS and Windows FT_Get_BDF_Charset_ID,
FT_Get_BDF_Property and FT_GlyphSlot_Embolden, _Oblique, _Slant and
_AdjustWeight were declared and not there: an application calling them
failed to link. They are compiled everywhere but Android now.

--- a/third_party/freetype/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/freetype/BUILD.gn
@@ -137,7 +137,9 @@
     ]
   }
 
-  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_cast_android) {
+  # zebkit: on every system, as its <freetype/ftbdf.h> and
+  # <freetype/ftsynth.h> are on every system (zebkit_vendor_freetype_*).
+  if (!is_android || is_cast_android) {
     # Needed for content_shell on Linux and Chromecast, since fontconfig
     # requires FT_Get_BDF_Property.
     sources += [ "src/src/base/ftbdf.c" ]
